### **Project Overview and My Role**

I was the lead designer on the project. The first phase redesigned the car-buying flows. The online store offers three different ways to buy a car, so three different flows had to be designed.

I began by defining the purchase journey from a user-centered perspective, from the site’s homepage all the way to the thank-you page. The multi-step redesign of the purchase flows required several rounds of wireframes and testing.

The second phase moved on to the brand redesign, which was rolled out across the entire site. Following corporate acquisitions, the existing site had to be updated to match the look and feel of the new international player. The visual guidelines for the Ayvens brand were provided, but I also had to adapt them to suit an online store that differs significantly from the brand’s other sites. I built an extensive UI library in Figma, which made the site’s technical implementation straightforward.

Alongside the brand and purchase-flow overhaul, the site also received an updated content structure, a product page for cars for sale, and numerous usability and accessibility improvements.

### **Collaboration**

This large project was also heavily content-driven. Together with a content strategist, we built the sitemap, wrote UX copy, and planned content cross-linking and SEO visibility. We added a lot of guiding copy to the purchase flows and made information easier to find. The client trusted us as experts and gave us a great deal of freedom in the implementation. We presented progress weekly, and the final site went to the international organization’s brand guardians for approval before launch.

### **Distinctive Features of the Project**

The brand was being renewed worldwide, which dictated a tight, inflexible schedule. It also set the boundaries for localization and implementation choices. Through good collaboration with the various parties, we delivered solutions that met all of these requirements. The client was extremely happy with the project, and we received praise internationally as well. The Finnish approach to selling cars online has drawn particular attention elsewhere in Europe.
